WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.880
The National Rifle Association has been

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.880
one of the most powerful,
if not the most powerful,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.493
lobbying groups in America.

00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:12.840
The NRA is very powerful,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.500
not just because it has a lot of money,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.560
but because it has a lot of sway

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.050
with single issue pro-gun voters.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.769
It says that it has about
five million members

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.240
committed to gun ownership
and the Second Amendment.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.970
We're all just wanting to exercise

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.496
our Second Amendment rights
to protect ourselves,

00:00:31.496 --> 00:00:33.260
protect our property.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.340
I love the NRA.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.338
I love the Second Amendment.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.360
They've mobilized the single
issue voter on this topic,

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.080
up and down the entire ballot.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.236
And they've successfully
done that for years.

00:00:45.236 --> 00:00:46.553
There's a shooting, there's a shooting!

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.780
Gun violence in America.
Yes.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.993
We need more guns.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.460
But at the peak of its power,

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.470
the NRA finds itself besieged by scandals

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.580
and legal challenges that
threaten its very existence.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.369
Executives of the NRA are accused of

00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:08.870
looting the powerful gun rights groups

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.210
to the tune of millions of dollars.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.410
Gun owners across America
should be horrified

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.930
by what I saw inside of the NRA.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.172
An unchecked corporation
with too much power.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.230
It's fighting against attorneys general

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:26.180
in New York, in Washington DC.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.870
It's fighting a legal battle

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.570
against its former advertising agency.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.850
It's spending millions and millions

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.853
of dollars on legal bills.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.380
There was a vicious civil war

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.380
between Wayne LaPierre and Oliver North.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.280
And it was very dramatic,
and very expensive.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.600
It has had large-scale layoffs.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.050
And it does seem that the NRA
is having a lot of trouble.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.930
While trouble does not necessarily

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.920
mean their ultimate
demise, there is no doubt

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.443
that in recent years, the
NRA shot itself in the foot.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.260
The NRA wasn't always all-powerful,

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.430
or even political for that matter.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:19.130
The NRA was formed in 1871
by two former Union soldiers.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.960
Many people in the North just
didn't know how to use guns.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.637
And so the NRA's mission was
to train people how to use guns

00:02:25.637 --> 00:02:28.090
in the event there's another war.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.820
It remained a non-controversial

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.090
gun safety organization
for over a hundred years.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.100
Its earliest foray into
politics can be traced back to

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.610
the National Firearms Act in 1934.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.830
This major piece of
gun control legislation

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.050
was actually supported by the NRA.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.123
Something the NRA of today
would consider heresy.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.200
It would take another five
decades for the humble nonprofit

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.720
to transform into a pro-gun lobby group

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.003
and ardent opponent of gun
regulations it is today.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:02.100
So the NRA became a little more political

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.700
starting in the 1970s,
and really ramped up

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.860
its political efforts
throughout the '80s and '90s.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.930
Pushing back on any efforts
by states or Congress

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.740
to restrict gun rights
through background checks

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.283
or waiting periods before
guns could be purchased.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.653
From my cold dead hands!

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.080
The NRA raises its money
from membership fees

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.110
and donations from wealthy individuals

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.463
and gun manufacturers.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.720
But it isn't just one simple

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.463
nonprofit organization anymore.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.450
Along with its political
transformation came a multitude

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.650
of offshoot foundations
for varying purposes.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.540
Well, what we call the NRA is really

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.670
a number of different organizations.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.930
It has a political spending arm

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.420
and it has a charitable foundation.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.560
The organizations have
to keep separate books,

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.690
but they don't have to operate

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.300
fully independently of one another.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.480
And indeed, they're all
basically run by Wayne LaPierre,

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.053
the head of the NRA.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.540
Wayne LaPierre is basically a walking,

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.400
talking iteration of the
National Rifle Association.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.040
He's not a avid shooter
himself, but nonetheless

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.970
he's been a very effective
lobbyist for gun rights,

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.700
and been a very effective
spokesperson for the NRA.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.590
We're never gonna stop
fighting for your right,

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.670
and folks just like you all over America,

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.663
to have the right to defend themselves.

00:04:34.155 --> 00:04:35.698
Newtown 911, what's the location

00:04:35.698 --> 00:04:37.531
of your emergency?
Sandy Hook School,

00:04:37.531 --> 00:04:39.900
I think there's somebody's
shooting in here.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.220
LaPierre became somewhat of

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.690
a household name in 2012,
when he offered a defensive

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.640
and seemingly tone-deaf response

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.800
to the school massacre at Sandy Hook.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.800
The only thing that stops
a bad guy with a gun

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.175
is a good guy with a gun.

00:04:57.175 --> 00:04:59.510
The NRA stop killing our children.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:03.009
The NRA does best when it's under attack.

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:04.207
The NRA has blood on its hands!

00:05:06.747 --> 00:05:08.950
During the Obama administration,

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.950
you had a spate of tragic mass
killings in the United States

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:17.720
and this put the gun
world on the defensive.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.840
USA, USA, USA!

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:24.950
When people feel that their
access or their ability

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.840
to obtain and keep guns is threatened,

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.430
that's when they support the
National Rifle Association.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.220
And indeed, it was boom time

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.600
for both NRA membership enrollment
and gun sales in America.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.560
Under the leadership of
LaPierre, the NRA was credited

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.370
for defeating President
Obama's legislative agenda

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:47.440
for stronger gun regulations
in his second term.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.800
All in all, this was a pretty
shameful day for Washington.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.170
And of course, the NRA was

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.573
an early backer of the Trump campaign.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.173
The Second Amendment is so important.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.600
They're not gonna take
your guns away, folks.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.337
They're not gonna take the
guns away, not gonna do it.

00:06:06.337 --> 00:06:11.337
The NRA went to great pains
to get Donald Trump elected.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.587
I'm officially announcing
the NRA's endorsement

00:06:13.587 --> 00:06:15.643
of Donald Trump for president.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:20.980
And they were able to amass very large

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.510
sums of money for Donald
Trump, $30 million.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:28.890
And about $54 million
for the entire election.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.010
And they were very successful.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:33.940
The election of Donald
Trump in November, 2016,

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:37.993
seemed to signal that the NRA
was at the peak of its power.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.800
High on its own success,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.850
the NRA ventured to launch NRATV,

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.710
an ambitious online
media network dedicated

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:51.710
not only to gun culture, but
to the culture wars in general,

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.550
Satan hates everything good about America.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.383
So does Kaepernick.

00:06:55.383 --> 00:06:57.430
Men were made to create.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.102
They were made to conquer.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.400
Much of NRATV was filled
with right wing screeds

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.780
against immigration, against journalists,

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.320
against fake news, against liberals.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.690
Not all Muslims are radicalized,

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:16.340
but all radicalized
terrorists are Muslims.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:17.800
But NRATV turned out

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.730
to be a resounding failure.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:21.730
I never would have imagined

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:24.420
these little neat pockets
and hidden closures.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.500
Not that many people were watching it.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.160
And it was very expensive
for the NRA to produce.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.660
The answer to the question,
what the is NRATV,

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.040
is it's just a vessel
to sell America guns.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.580
That's pretty much it.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.950
NRATV was a bad business
decision for the NRA.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.933
It costs the NRA
something like $40 million

00:07:44.933 --> 00:07:47.420
and got very, very few viewers.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:49.850
The failure of NRATV eventually

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.180
came back to haunt them
and ultimately led to

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.060
the first real signs of
trouble for the foundation.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.850
I see it, it was the white hoods

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.090
and the burning train tracks.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.990
Okay, fine, fair point.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.230
Now I should warn you,

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.583
this is where things get complicated.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:11.550
The NRA's troubles really
began in October of 2017,

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.460
when New York State
launched an investigation

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.190
into an insurance product
called Carry Guard.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:19.680
And it turned out the NRA
didn't have the right permits

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.140
under New York insurance law
to be selling this insurance.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.490
And that would cause the
NRA to hire a new lawyer,

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.580
a fellow by the name of William Brewer.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.560
He warned that the NRA was
likely to be further investigated

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.040
by the State of New York.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.950
Brewer suggested that the NRA conduct

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.300
a full-scale internal audit to ensure

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.680
their books were in order,
a large part of which

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.160
involved tracking the
enormous expenditures

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.490
incurred by their longtime
PR agency, Ackerman McQueen.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.380
Among other PR services rendered

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.420
during their decades-long relationship,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:54.380
Ackerman McQueen billed $40
million for the NRATV project.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.100
This included a large undisclosed salary

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.660
to then NRA president Oliver North,

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.520
theoretically an unpaid position,

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.260
for his appearances on NRATV.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:07.790
I spent my life with those
who relish a good, fair fight.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.310
He was making a salary of apparently

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.260
over a million dollars a year.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:16.400
And the NRA said, we need
to review that contract.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.110
But it's really only
the tip of the iceberg.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.330
It turns out that the NRA

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.400
and Ackerman McQueen had
profound disagreements.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:28.400
Ackerman McQueen responded
by detailing to the public

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.880
that Wayne LaPierre and other people

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.420
who were at the head of the
NRA were taking advantage of

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:38.090
the NRA's charitable status,
using it for personal expenses.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.680
Such as expensive travel to the Bahamas,

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.700
shopping trips in Beverly Hills,

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:43.950
where Wayne LaPierre would spend

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.750
hundreds of thousands of dollars.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.830
And it even came out that Wayne LaPierre

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.903
had a secret $17 million
golden parachute contract.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.780
Oliver North had been
pressing the NRA's board

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.490
to investigate the NRA's expenditures,

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.070
including with Ackerman McQueen,

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.873
and even the NRA's law firm.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.850
In April of 2019, the NRA filed a lawsuit

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.020
against Ackerman McQueen for over-billing

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.490
and lack of transparency, just days before

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.990
The New Yorker dropped a bombshell report,

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:16.710
alleging corruption on a staggering scale.

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:20.050
With a particular focus on
the questionable relationship

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.770
between Ackerman McQueen and the NRA.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:25.350
So the New York attorney
general alleges that the NRA

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.820
was using Ackerman McQueen's expenses

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:32.230
to enrich its leadership
through improper spending.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.520
The New Yorker article quoted

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.932
a former IRS official
in charge of overseeing

00:10:35.932 --> 00:10:38.500
tax exempt organizations as saying that

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.120
the NRA had a litany of red flags

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.220
that were "just extraordinary."

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.680
Ackerman McQueen and Oliver North

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.890
have not responded to
requests for comment.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.940
And in court filings, Ackerman McQueen

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:53.000
has denied the NRA allegations.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.210
Thank you so much.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.440
All this acrimony made for

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:01.100
a tense annual NRA meeting,
the following week.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:04.060
Oliver North threatened Wayne LaPierre.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.100
Said he would disclose information

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.810
about his incredible spending

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.230
with the NRA's money on personal expenses

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.350
if Wayne LaPierre didn't step down

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.580
from leadership of the organization.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.180
LaPierre quickly retaliated
and accused North

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.850
and Ackerman McQueen of
trying to carry out a coup.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.750
Oliver North brought
his issue to the board.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.150
But when the board meeting ended,

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.760
Wayne LaPierre was still there.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.370
And Oliver North was out as president.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.640
And indeed, in the months to come,

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.510
Wayne LaPierre would purge virtually

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.330
all of the Ackerman McQueen supporters,

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.920
including Chris Cox, the head of the NRA's

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.680
legislative arm and lobbying arm.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.853
And before long, LaPierre
was standing alone.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:51.040
But for LaPierre, it
was a Pyrrhic victory.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.860
So the internal fight was over,

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.980
but it had the effect of
triggering what became

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.780
the New York attorney general's
lawsuit against the NRA.

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:03.010
Enter Letitia James,
the new sheriff in town.

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:05.270
So Letitia James is a Democrat.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.670
And she was elected back in 2018 to become

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.230
New York's top law enforcement officer.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:14.040
James ran on a platform of
challenging Donald Trump.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.360
But she was also highly
critical of the NRA,

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:19.210
which she accused of being
a terrorist organization.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:23.270
A claim that the NRA claims
is defamatory and false.

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.510
But it was the revelations
that came out of

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.670
the Ackerman McQueen lawsuit that really

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:31.070
provided her a basis to go after the NRA.

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:33.460
So Attorney General James
rolled up her sleeves

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:36.840
and dug in, obtaining sworn
testimony from key players,

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.430
including Oliver North.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:41.200
And reviewing thousands
of pages of documents,

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.230
many of which the NRA
attempted to withhold from her.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:46.900
Especially when it came to
any information pertaining to

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.340
their relationship with Ackerman McQueen.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:51.800
But eventually James had seen enough.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.240
It's clear that the NRA has
been failing to carry out

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.560
its stated mission for many, many years.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:01.343
And instead has operated as
a breeding ground for greed,

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:07.450
abuse, and brazen illegality.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:10.060
The NRA has denied New York's allegations,

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.680
calling the lawsuit a baseless

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.910
political attack on the organization.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:16.450
Around the same time that
New York filed its lawsuit,

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.270
the District of Columbia
attorney general, Karl Racine,

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:22.410
also a Democrat, filed a
separate lawsuit against the NRA

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:26.040
and the NRA foundation, accusing
the foundation of allowing

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:29.360
charitable funds to be
used for improper purposes.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.270
On October 19th, 2020,

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.540
the NRA filed a response to the New York

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.050
attorney general's lawsuit asking to have

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:39.140
the case dismissed,
calling it the capstone of

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:42.150
a partisan election interference project.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.490
It's anyone's guess when the judge

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.300
will respond to the NRA's request.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.800
And this really is just
the beginning of the case.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.460
What we do know is that the NRA

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.960
has been hemorrhaging
money on fees to combat

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.670
ongoing legal battles on
every imaginable front.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:01.120
Part of the NRA's financial situation

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.570
comes from incredible legal fees.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.840
William Brewer and his law
firm have been charging

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:09.920
the NRA more than $1.3 million a month.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.450
A filing by Ackerman claims
that Brewer's law firm

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.370
has collected $54 million in the two years

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.803
of representing the NRA.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:20.070
In a leaked audio recording, LaPierre told

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.110
surviving board members that the NRA

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:24.267
is in serious financial trouble.

00:14:24.267 --> 00:14:27.343
The cost that we bore was probably about

00:14:27.343 --> 00:14:30.802
a hundred million dollar
hit in lost revenue

00:14:30.802 --> 00:14:32.103
in 2018 and 2019.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.900
That was back in January, 2020,

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:38.960
before the filings in
New York State and DC.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.930
Not to mention the layoffs it's had to do

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:43.090
after the Coronavirus outbreak.

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:46.950
So they can only expect to
keep spending a lot more.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:50.320
To add insult to injury,
recently ousted Joshua Powell

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.170
has released a tell-all
book with firsthand accounts

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:56.080
of alleged misconduct across the board.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.410
It is an abomination of members' money

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.750
that what's gone on
over the past 30 years.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.770
It's to the tune of hundreds of millions

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.360
of dollars in wastage.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.790
The allegations make you seem like

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.140
part of the problem though.

00:15:09.179 --> 00:15:10.540
I understand that.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:13.900
He's blaming his own misdeeds in many ways

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:17.310
as just part of the culture of the NRA.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.560
And indeed it does appear
increasingly likely

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.430
that there was a culture at the NRA

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:24.380
where leadership basically
treated the organization

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.780
like a personal piggy bank.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.570
The NRA rejected Powell's allegations.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.840
So right now, the NRA
is in full defense mode.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:35.150
This means that millions
of dollars that the NRA

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:37.940
would normally spend on
lobbying and donations

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:41.130
is being spent instead on
law firms and legal fees.

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:43.930
Just at a time when they're
fighting for their survival.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.230
There's no ending to this story yet.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.610
And it's far too soon
for the NRA's enemies

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.520
to do a victory lap.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.090
LaPierre is working hard to paint himself

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.000
and the organization as the victim

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.300
of vicious partisan attacks.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.650
If they think they're getting our guns,

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:06.233
I'm just telling 'em, 1776
is gonna kick off again!

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.870
The NRA is using these existential threats

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.010
to gin up support and
raise the money needed

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.140
to dig itself out of dire straits,

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.820
beat all the cases against it,

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.920
and come out stronger than ever.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.910
Although the attorney general has sought

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.440
to dissolve the NRA, that does seem like

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.010
an unlikely ultimate outcome from this.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.460
I think it is very possible
that the NRA will be hit with

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.090
significant fines and be forced to remove

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.362
certain members of the
board, like Wayne LaPierre.

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.660
Regardless of the outcome,

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:37.670
there's a universal
lesson to be learned here,

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:39.510
as old as time itself.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.500
The NRA's downfall seems likely

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:44.730
to come from its own hubris.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.910
One of the dangers of
being the most powerful

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.730
political organization in America

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:51.230
is you feel that no one can beat you.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:53.500
But New York attorney
general Letitia James

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.300
has got something to say about that.

